  "rendered": "The largest particle size in Table 2[1] is 625 ±58 nm[2]. It belongs to the LF-RES[3] nanoparticles, which deliver silncOSLMT[4] (ref. [118][5]). The smallest is 53.42 ±4.63[6] nm, from an MMP-2-responsive peptide system carrying siPD-L1[7] (ref. [219][8]).\n\nSubtracting the mean values gives a difference of about 571.58[9] nm, so the largest is roughly an order of magnitude bigger. This leaves out the reported ± variations. Some entries are given only as approximate values (\"~\") or upper bounds (\"<\"), and a few have no size listed. None of those is larger than the largest or smaller than the smallest value above.",
